C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:32:     - `prior_debates` (**M1 — resurface failed/accepted directions, 2026-06-16**): in **generation 1 only**, run `python -m cli.debate_aggregate --topic "<2-4 key terms from the topic>" --format planner-context` and include its stdout verbatim (empty stdout ⇒ include nothing). This deterministic reader surfaces prior debates on a similar topic — REJECTED/STALLED directions (do NOT re-propose as-is without addressing why they failed) + ACCEPTED decisions (you MAY build on). **Advisory only — the Planner weighs it; it NEVER auto-vetoes a proposal.** Closes the previously dead-end `cli.debate_aggregate.aggregate()` reader (write side wired, read side 0); mirrors AutoScientists "preserve + resurface success/failure to cut redundant exploration". Later generations already carry `prior_generation`/`critic_feedback`, so skip there.
